    <string name="notes_calculation_help_action">Calculation information</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_title">Calculations in Notes</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_syntax_title">Syntax</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_syntax_body">Each operation must start with an = sign. You can leave spaces immediately after the sign, but write the expression without spaces.\nExample: Purchase = 10+2*3</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_rules_title">Rules</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_rules_body">• Available operators: +, -, * and /.\n• You can use a comma or a period for decimals.\n• Multiplication and division are calculated before addition and subtraction.\n• Negative values are supported, for example: =-10+2.\n• Parentheses and percentages are not supported.\n• Invalid expressions and division by zero are not calculated.</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_examples_title">Examples</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_examples_body">Food =10+2*3  →  16\nTransport =4.5/2  →  2.25\n\nWhen the note is displayed, the result appears next to each operation.</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_total_title">Total</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_total_body">The Total adds the results of every valid operation in the text. In the example above it is 18.25. It updates while you edit the note.</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_checklist_title">Checklist calculations</string>
    <string name="notes_calculation_help_checklist_body">Only the first operation in each task is counted. The description and the opening or closing notes are not included in the calculation.\n\nExample:\n☑ Bread =2+3\n☐ Milk =4\nTotal: 9 · Pending: 4\n\nTotal includes every task. Pending subtracts checked tasks and updates when you check or uncheck items.</string>
